  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that PCA-based RNA with multiprofile avgpool is the best current setting (accuracy 0.591, F1 0.573), clearly above singleprofile PCA and transformer aggregation, while image-only ResNet is weak. The key uncertainty is whether a stronger single-cell RNA representation can improve this best RNA-only baseline. config_008 tests scGPT under the same multiprofile avgpool setting, changing only the RNA encoder, so it isolates representation quality. This is a high-value next step because it exploits the strongest known direction, has plausible immediate performance, and avoids confounding RNA improvements with image or fusion choices before the RNA component is better understood."
